/* V93 — two doors.

   ---- What the home screen currently asks ----

   Six buttons, all the same size, all worded like the headline feature of a different game:

     CAMPAIGN            15 stages • continue where you stopped
     QUICK DUEL          LIVE MATCHMAKING READY
     DAILY ARENA         One field. Everyone gets the same one.
     SOLO ASCENSION      Endless waves • escalating missions
     TITAN GAUNTLET      Boss rush • maximum pressure
     PLAY WITH FRIENDS   Private invite, room code or public arena

   A player opening this for the first time has to read six subtitles and pick, before they have any
   idea what any of the words mean, and nothing on the screen tells them which one is the game. Two
   of the six are the same thing — QUICK DUEL and PLAY WITH FRIENDS are both "play against a person",
   split by how you find them, which is an implementation detail the player is being asked to decide
   before they have a rival. And three more are variations on the run loop that only mean anything to
   somebody who has already played it: "endless waves" is not a promise you can evaluate having never
   seen one wave.

   The cost is not aesthetic. This screen is the first thing anyone sees, the decision is made with
   the least information they will ever have, and five of the six answers are wrong for a new player.

   ---- Two ----

     PLAY   continues the campaign — the map, your stage, where you were.
     DUEL   a rival, whether that is matchmaking or a friend's invite.

   PLAY plays. It does not open a submenu, because a button that says PLAY and then asks another
   question is the same problem one level deeper. Pressing it goes to the map, and the map already
   has your current node lit as the thing to press — V88 built that, and it means the campaign's
   "where was I" is answered by a picture rather than by a sentence.

   ---- Nothing is deleted ----

   The daily arena, endless and the gauntlet are all still here, one level down, on the map screen —
   which is where you are once you have pressed PLAY and is exactly the population that knows what
   those words mean. They are three chips rather than three huge buttons because that is their honest
   weight: they are what you do with the game once you have it, not what the game is.

   Quick match moves onto the duel screen, alongside the invite and the room code, which is where it
   always belonged: those three are one decision ("who am I playing?") that was split across two
   levels of the menu.

   ---- Built by forwarding, not by rewiring ----

   Every one of the six buttons stays in the DOM with its handler attached, and the new controls
   click them. That is the same choice V90 made with the results screen and for the same reasons: the
   rules about what each mode does are already correct and already tested, V39 writes the daily's hint
   into `#dailyBtnHint` and V29 writes the network's state into `.mode-live-copy` without knowing this
   part exists, and a consolidation that reimplemented six entry points would be six new places for
   them to disagree. `.click()` works on a hidden element, so hiding them costs nothing. */

const V93={on:true};

let v93Play=null;
let v93Duel=null;

function v93Fire(id){
 const el=$(id);
 if(el)el.click();
}

/* The one sentence that has to be true on this screen: where PLAY will take you. Read live rather
   than stored, because the campaign advances from inside a run and the menu is rebuilt on return. */
function v93Where(){
 const map=(typeof v87Map==='function')?v87Map():null;
 const stage=(typeof v14Save==='object'&&v14Save)?(v14Save.lastStage|0):0;
 const total=(typeof v14StageCount!=='undefined')?v14StageCount:15;
 const place=map?map.name:'THE OUTER REACH';
 if(stage<=1)return `${place} — START AT THE BEGINNING`;
 return `${place} — STAGE ${Math.min(stage,total)} OF ${total}`;
}

function v93Build(){
 if(v93Play||!V93.on)return;
 const old=document.querySelector('.mode-command');
 if(!old)return;

 /* Given its own container next to `.mode-command` rather than placed inside it, and this is the
    second attempt: the first put the doors in the existing block and lost. Four stylesheets have
    been layered onto that block over the life of this project and three of them use `!important` —
    `.mode-command{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))!important}` in v15-vision,
    `#menuScreen .mode-command .huge{min-height:96px!important}` in v19-craft — so the two doors
    came out as a matched pair of blue tiles 96px tall whatever this part asked for.

    Winning that would have meant a fifth layer of `!important` on the same selectors, which is how
    a stylesheet becomes unmaintainable one reasonable decision at a time. A sibling container
    inherits none of it, and the old block is hidden with its six buttons and their handlers intact
    inside — which is the arrangement this part wanted anyway. */
 const host=document.createElement('div');
 host.className='v93-doors';
 old.parentNode.insertBefore(host,old);

 /* No icons, and that is a decision rather than an omission. The six-button screen used one glyph
    per mode to help tell them apart, which is work two buttons do not need — and the glyphs were
    never safe: the crossed-swords this started with rendered as an empty box on the test device,
    because a mode menu is not somewhere to find out which symbols a phone's font actually has.
    PLAY and DUEL are unambiguous words. */
 const make=(id,cls,label)=>{
  const b=document.createElement('button');
  b.id=id;
  b.className=cls;
  b.type='button';
  b.innerHTML=`<b></b><small></small>`;
  b.querySelector('b').textContent=label;
  return b;
 };

 /* No `primary`/`secondary`/`huge` either: those are exactly the classes the four layers above
    target, and these two buttons are styled outright in v93-two.css. */
 v93Play=make('v93PlayBtn','v93-door','PLAY');
 v93Duel=make('v93DuelBtn','v93-door','DUEL');
 v93Play.addEventListener('click',()=>{haptic(12);v93Fire('campaignBtn');});
 v93Duel.addEventListener('click',()=>{haptic(12);v93Fire('socialBtn');});
 host.prepend(v93Duel);
 host.prepend(v93Play);
 v93Paint();
}

function v93Paint(){
 if(!v93Play)return;
 v93Play.querySelector('small').textContent=v93Where();
 /* Mirrored rather than duplicated: V29 keeps the live copy honest about whether the network is
    actually up, and inventing a second sentence here would be a second thing to keep true. */
 const live=document.querySelector('#quickBtn .mode-live-copy');
 const copy=live?live.textContent.trim():'';
 v93Duel.querySelector('small').textContent=copy&&/READY|LIVE/i.test(copy)
  ? 'FIND A RIVAL, OR INVITE A FRIEND'
  : 'INVITE A FRIEND, OR JOIN A ROOM';
}

const v93UpdateMenu=updateMenu;
updateMenu=function(){
 const out=v93UpdateMenu();
 if(V93.on){v93Build();v93Paint();}
 return out;
};

/* ---- The three chips, on the map --------------------------------------------------------------

   Rebuilt with the map rather than parked next to it: `v14RenderStages` clears `#stageList` and
   fills it from scratch on every map change and every stage cleared, so anything inserted once
   would survive exactly until the first thing the player does. */

const V93_RAIL=[
 {id:'soloBtn',   label:'ENDLESS', hint:()=>{
  const f=(typeof v90Field==='function')?v90Field():null;
  return f&&f.best>0?`BEAT ${format(f.best)}`:'ONE FIELD, UNTIL YOU BEAT IT';
 }},
 {id:'dailyBtn',  label:'TODAY',   hint:()=>{
  const h=$('dailyBtnHint');
  return h&&h.textContent.trim()?h.textContent.trim():'EVERYONE GETS THE SAME FIELD';
 }},
 {id:'gauntletBtn',label:'TITANS', hint:()=>'BOSSES ONLY, BACK TO BACK'}
];

function v93Rail(){
 const list=$('stageList');
 if(!V93.on||!list)return;
 if(list.querySelector('.v93-rail'))return;
 const head=list.querySelector('.v88-head');
 const rail=document.createElement('div');
 rail.className='v93-rail';
 rail.append(Object.assign(document.createElement('span'),{className:'v93-rail-label',textContent:'OTHER WAYS IN'}));
 const row=document.createElement('div');
 row.className='v93-rail-row';
 for(const entry of V93_RAIL){
  const chip=document.createElement('button');
  chip.type='button';
  chip.className='v93-rail-chip';
  chip.innerHTML=`<b></b><small></small>`;
  chip.querySelector('b').textContent=entry.label;
  chip.querySelector('small').textContent=entry.hint();
  chip.addEventListener('click',()=>{haptic(12);v93Fire(entry.id);});
  row.append(chip);
 }
 rail.append(row);
 if(head&&head.nextSibling)list.insertBefore(rail,head.nextSibling);
 else list.append(rail);
}

if(typeof v14RenderStages==='function'){
 const v93RenderStages=v14RenderStages;
 v14RenderStages=function(){
  const out=v93RenderStages();
  v93Rail();
  return out;
 };
}

/* ---- Quick match, moved onto the duel screen ---------------------------------------------------

   The screen already asks "who am I playing?" three ways and was missing the fourth, which was up on
   the home screen as a coequal mode. Placed above the grid rather than in it because it is the
   answer for a player with nobody in particular to play — the other three all require somebody you
   already know. */

function v93Quick(){
 /* getElementById rather than `$`, and not a style choice: the build validates that every id `$` is
    called with exists in index.html, which is a good rule and this element is built at runtime. */
 if(!V93.on||document.getElementById('v93QuickBtn'))return;
 const screen=$('socialScreen');
 const grid=screen&&screen.querySelector('.social-grid');
 if(!grid)return;
 const btn=document.createElement('button');
 btn.id='v93QuickBtn';
 btn.type='button';
 btn.className='primary huge v93-quick';
 btn.innerHTML='<b>QUICK MATCH</b><small>One tap. We pair you with the next pilot looking for one.</small>';
 btn.addEventListener('click',()=>{haptic(12);v93Fire('quickBtn');});
 grid.parentNode.insertBefore(btn,grid);

 /* The screen a door opens should be named after the door. This one has been called "ENTER THE
    ARENA" under an eyebrow reading "FRIENDLY AND OPEN PLAY" since before there was a DUEL button to
    press, and a player who taps DUEL and lands somewhere with neither word on it has to re-read the
    screen to check they did what they meant to. */
 const eyebrow=screen.querySelector('.eyebrow');
 const title=screen.querySelector('h2');
 if(eyebrow)eyebrow.textContent='WHO ARE YOU PLAYING?';
 if(title)title.textContent='DUEL';
}

const v93ShowScreen=showScreen;
showScreen=function(id){
 const out=v93ShowScreen(id);
 if(V93.on&&id==='socialScreen')v93Quick();
 return out;
};

/* Built once at load as well as on the first `updateMenu`, because the menu is the screen the game
   opens on and a player who never triggers an update would otherwise see an empty command block. */
v93Build();
